# Build directories. The glob, not just "build/", so a second tree for a
# clean-configure check (build-clean/, build-msvc/) is ignored too: those
# hold absolute paths from the machine that configured them.
#
# LEADING SLASH, so it matches only at the repo root. Unanchored, "build*/"
# also matched src/services/builders/ — anything whose name merely starts with
# "build" — and new source files added there were silently never committed.
/build*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# IDE files
.vs/
.vscode/
.claude/
.cache/
*.vcxproj.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
.idea/

# Compiled files
*.obj
*.o
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

# CMake generated
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
compile_commands.json

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ImGui layout file (user-specific)
imgui.ini

# Packaged distributions (tools/package-linux.sh) — hundreds of MB, all reproducible
/dist/

# Python bytecode from the build/codegen helper scripts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
